  "text": "Beneath the lamps’ ethereal, pale light,\nHe walked the streets of the city’s night.\nEach step echoed on pavement stone,\nA solitary, rhythmic tone.\n\nLike ghosts, the people drifted by,\nWith vacant eyes and passing sigh.\nTheir faces buried, deep and far,\nIn worlds that held them near and far.\n\nAmidst the urban, heaving sea,\nHe felt the weight of solitude.\n\nThe animal known for its long neck is the giraffe."
